# A static site has no server of its own, so it has no secrets and needs no .env to run.
# Its public build settings (VITE_ values) go in .env.production (committed), not here: Vite never
# reads .env.example, and .dockerignore keeps .env out of the image build. Vite bakes every VITE_
# value into the JavaScript, where any visitor can read it: never an API key or another secret.
# Anything secret belongs on a server, which means another forge profile.

# Only for docker compose, in a .env file: the port on this machine (127.0.0.1 only) where
# docker-compose.yml publishes the site, when 8080 is taken.
# APP_PORT=8080
